From e7943b738c587ae2b397bd7b9935637fe07b1348 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/49] R4: CompressionAuto decides from the encoder's output
 for the whole blob; the sampler is removed

The sampler encoded 16 windows of 2 KiB and stored the blob uncompressed
when they did not shrink by 1%. Redundancy outside or between the windows
was missed: one incompressible 64 KiB block sixteen times was stored at
1,048,608 bytes where stock stores 65,661. No decision that looks at a part
of the blob can exclude this, and a pass that can costs what the encoder
costs, so every blob is encoded again, as in stock.

What remains of ruling 2 is exact: a data blob of 512 KiB or more is kept
uncompressed if and only if the encoder's output plus the four-byte length
field of a compressed entry is not smaller than the blob. What is stored is
never larger than what stock stores, and a blob that the encoder shrinks is
stored byte for byte as stock stores it.

The league's test of the removed function goes with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
